title: Run CI on self-hosted runners with scoped Cargo compiler caching

doc:
  - audience:
      - Node Dev
      - Node Operator
    description: |
      GitHub workflows use the existing Atleta-network self-hosted runner group.
      Supported Rust job containers and Docker builders use the group compiler
      cache with pinned sccache and temporary trusted configuration forwarding.
      Cache access is restricted by the existing pull-request trust boundary.
      Each runner keeps an isolated workspace and tool storage; build targets
      are not shared between concurrent jobs. PRdoc Python tools install into a
      private temporary environment with their required YAML parser.
      Native Cargo jobs omit archive-cache cleanup that can delete shared crate
      sources; archive caching remains only inside isolated job containers.

      Existing toolchains, compiler arguments, test partitions, release gates
      and final runtime stages are preserved. Native macOS ARM64 and oldlinux
      lanes require matching self-hosted capacity. Full SDK build and release
      validation remains required before this infrastructure change is merged.

crates: []
